#2024/11/27: Mano
# First fetch files from Glygen by 

go to folder: 000_raw_files_from_GlyGen

and run

./fetch.sh

The downloaded files have current date in their name. Go to the parent (this) folder. 

In the next script, zz00_convert_CSV.pl, change the date accordingly in one of the file names, e.g., the line:

#my $inFile = '000_raw_files_from_GlyGen/glycan_pubchem_status-2024-11-26.csv';
my $inFile = '000_raw_files_from_GlyGen/glycan_pubchem_status-2025-08-15.csv';

Changed the shebang line to:
#!/usr/bin/perl
##!/usr/local/bin/perl

Then, run it as
./zz00_convert_CSV.pl

Then, run the other two as (in sequence, after the previous one completes):

./zz01_load_pubchem_synonyms_to_insert.pl
./zz02_create_compound_records_for_uncovered_GlyTouCan_ACs.pl

All three perl scripts ran without any issues.


